1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://forum.arkivverket.no/topic/110249-24574-sally-batt-eller-rath-jahnsen-f-dartmouth-england-15021790-d-e-1865/
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. til innlegg (1)På FS finner jeg en Sarah Batt gift med Jacob Jansen 7 nov 1809, St Marys, Portsea, Hampshire, England.Jeg tror at Sally kann brukes på en som er døpt til Sarah.En Salley Batt blev døpt 9 april 1791 i St Petrox
2 CONC , Dartmouth, Devon, England med foreldre Henry Batt og Sarah, ifølge samme kilde. Mulige søsken: George Henry Graham B. 15/11 1789 samme sted, Henry B. 24/7 1796, s.s., William Courtney B. 28/2 1794,s.s.Og hvis Salley 1791 er rett
2 CONC  kannskje hennes foreldre er Henry Batt g. Sarah Vinnay , St Petrox, Dartmouth 11 matrs 1789 (fortsatt FS). Og da er evt.http://genforum.gene...m/batt/all.htmlnr. 253 og efterfølgende debatt av interesse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/batt/messages/381.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally Batt [daughter of Henry] was baptised at St Petrox Dartmouth England on April 9th 1791. Her brother Henry wes also baptised at the same place on the 24th July 1796. I believe Henry was my great great grandfather. I do not ha
2 CONC ve many details of Henry [snr] or Sarah Vinnay, but on page 2 of this forum site you will see details of Henry Batt and Susannah Slight. Carole Roberts whe responded to my search may be able to give you some information.
2 CONT
2 CONT best of luck Gerald Batt. http://genforum.genealogy.com/batt/messages/383.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Hello, further to Gerald Batt’s message I can tell you the following about Henry Batt who married Sarah Vinnay in Dartmouth 1789.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was said to be ‘of Alverstoke, Hants, mariner’. Two bits of circumstantial evidence make me believe that he was the Henry Batt who was baptised 1770 at Gosport, parents Henry Batt and Mary Cummins who married in 1769. I have
2 CONC  no information on Sarah Vinnay but there were quite a few Vinneys in Devon so she may well have come from there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Batt and Sarah Vinnay had 4 children baptised at St Petrox Dartmouth: George Henry Graham Batt 1789, Salley Batt 1791, William Courtney Batt 1794 (my ancestor) and Henry Batt 1796. There were no more Batt entries in the pari
2 CONC sh registers after this suggesting that the family then moved elsewhere.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1803 Henry and Sarah lived in Portsmouth. The John Batt baptised 1801 Gosport may also be their son but I have not been able to prove this.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1796 Henry became a lieutenant and after that he did act as captain of ships. Around late 1805 it was reported that ‘Henry Batt, late commander of the Albatross sloop, died on board The Trident 2 days before she reached The Dow
2 CONC ns from the East Indies’. His will was proved in July 1806. Unfortunately I have been unable to find a reference to Henry’s death in the Trident’s records and have not yet found his burial which would be very useful if it gave his
2 CONC  age.
2 CONT
2 CONT I know that in November 1809 Sally Batt married Jacob Janson or Jenson in Portsea, and that being a minor it was with the consent of her widowed mother Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have a few details of Henry’s naval career and more details of those of his sons William and Henry. If you think you are related to this family please let me know so that I can give you more information.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carole Roberts.
