2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Skattergade 10, Svendborg, Denmark
2 NOTE SKATTERGADE 10:
3 CONT
3 CONT At this place was in 1761 a 7 fags (parts of the buildings between 2 bars) 1 first floor forhus (front) of egebindingdværk (half-timbering) the roof of stone, which was rebuilt around 1780. The house had a driveway and a 3-fags at
3 CONC tic, the extension to the south was extended to a 2 Floor a total of 6 fag. Such is it today (1975).
3 CONT
3 CONT Entire façade, the ground floor and 1 floor in the eastern 6 fag is bindingsværk (half-timbering) with red painted woodwork and bright yellow in joints. The 2-fløjede fyldningsdør (2 wings panel doors) have cutting outs that are p
3 CONC ainted in blue, red and orange colors. The plinth of boulders are painted in the colors Cool Blue. the roof is in red bricks. The house stands as one of the best preserved and most well maintained "bindingdværks" houses in Svendbo
3 CONC rg giving Skattergades western terrace a special charm. The fine Louis-seize front door is definitely one of the most beautiful of Svendborgs main doors.
3 CONT FROM THE BOOK, 'REGISTRANT OVER BEVARINGSVÆRDIGE HUSE I SVENDBORG GAMLE KØBSTAD'
3 CONT
3 CONT Published 1975, page 213 (Register of worthy houses in the old Svendborg city):    (on file)
3 CONT
3 CONT    SKATTERGADE 10, Matr. nr. 499a Klasse B:
3 CONT
