2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Salve Johannessøn Kallevig (1732 – 4 February 1794) was a Norwegian businessperson. He is best known for founding the trading and shipping company Salve Kallevig & Søn in 1792, which was largely expanded by his son Morten Michael 
2 CONC Kallevig. The company was passed down through the generations, and existed until 1962.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * "Kallevig". Store norske leksikon (in Norwegian). Retrieved 16 May 2012.
2 CONT
