1 NAME Lars Larsen /Kleivaland/
2 GIVN Lars Larsen
2 SURN Kleivaland
2 _MARNM Myrene
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 APR 1822
2 ADDR
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 OCT 1895
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alt. birth 03 Mar 1820 (no proof) the proof supports the later birth date on 15 Apr 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Larson Myrene immigrated from Norway to the US in 1861 living in LaSalle and Livingston,Illinois for about 15 years , before moving to Wiota, Cass, Iowa in about 1876. He lived there till his death on 11 Oct 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars's birth date was off, see church records below
2 CONT Lars, born 15 April 1822, baptised 21 April in church, son of Lars Larsen and Brita Sjursdt. , Molandsvolden or Mälandsvolden.
2 CONT
2 CONT That combination of personal names and place name is pretty convincing to me; "Vollen under Meland" is just another way of expressing the idea contained in "Mälandsvolden" – the entity "Volden" or "Vollen" registered under the lar
2 CONC ger unit "Mäland". The information above is taken, as you will see, from the "Ministerialbok"; when I look up the parallel "Klokkerbok", it looks to me as if the place of abode for the Lars & Brita couple is "Wolden" – but the wri
2 CONC ting is very blurred so it is difficult to be certain.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Rasmus Larson was my great great grandfather.
